[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7194"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}-3{t}^{3}+t$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-10\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}-3{t}^{3}+t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{t}^{5}-\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=-10.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10 & =\\frac{1}{10}(0)^{5}-\\frac{3}{4}(0)^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}+C \\\\ -10 & =0+C \\\\ C & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{1}{10}{t}^{5}-\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-10.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =\\frac{1}{10}(2)^{5}-\\frac{3}{4}(2)^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}-10 \\\\  & =3.2-12+2-10 \\\\  & =-16.8\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $16.8\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-102695/selection/c8ad9bd48f88541e4e5dae671c020f866fe51c1cdb6f9415f4a543d8e6c677ed" :answer/id #uuid "0d646d2d-d0a2-5664-b3b5-7bce7237dbb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102695/selection/895e83c01da399938bc25ab193c6894e75966914fec968b8c399a51a4f9e8409" :answer/id #uuid "5b7dd7cc-fb99-51ea-97a0-eb8d633277ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{3}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102695/selection/e690edd27ab6c7016ca39ce1e80197beba90c9c714e1ef34fdad83199a2accb4" :answer/id #uuid "cf8ae0ad-6a77-5cc6-8614-51f744e4e77d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102695/selection/8089ba79580c5715626efca7b3e32c5951162e067f0cfd9038ba4d23c3ee58e3" :answer/id #uuid "ccc91e6c-78ce-5338-a817-e935063ab031" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102695/selection/75fcc058a039484bb434ae6e528332a89c278f2a0c3ba0d121ee77a5d31a81eb" :answer/id #uuid "8c2d4299-60d9-52ce-bf18-7322791f6eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102695/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e50b7e-7db3-5566-9a15-0ace852cb28d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102695/selection/8089ba79580c5715626efca7b3e32c5951162e067f0cfd9038ba4d23c3ee58e3" :answer-field/choices ["q-102695/selection/c8ad9bd48f88541e4e5dae671c020f866fe51c1cdb6f9415f4a543d8e6c677ed" "q-102695/selection/895e83c01da399938bc25ab193c6894e75966914fec968b8c399a51a4f9e8409" "q-102695/selection/e690edd27ab6c7016ca39ce1e80197beba90c9c714e1ef34fdad83199a2accb4" "q-102695/selection/8089ba79580c5715626efca7b3e32c5951162e067f0cfd9038ba4d23c3ee58e3" "q-102695/selection/75fcc058a039484bb434ae6e528332a89c278f2a0c3ba0d121ee77a5d31a81eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102695" :question/id #uuid "7b207322-8b81-50ed-8b36-b439725ea8bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-102695" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=2t+{t}^{2}$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{8}{3}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the velocity of the particle at the moment $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2t+{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=\\frac{8}{3}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3} & =(1)^{2}+\\frac{(1)^{3}}{3}+C \\\\ \\frac{8}{3} & =1+\\frac{1}{3}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{4}{3}+{t}^{2}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =\\frac{4}{3}+(2)^{2}+\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+4+\\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102695/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee2920dc-93e1-5595-a751-62ad5e4f3035"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81707/selection/fbe6d4c482d8e23104539942640ef1f21608bdba174b9d702ccbdc96fa6fe0c5" :answer/id #uuid "0798db24-5209-5971-8b62-6f9c2c116fbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=12{e}^{-t}-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81707/selection/0e76f3a88f14f467533c77e03d867e9385f96a31bae3dd4e69fef22acddc53a3" :answer/id #uuid "a55721e0-1b81-5593-821a-aff69e2b460c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=3{e}^{-2t}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81707/selection/e4997bc82e0286ae35edcde4ec9a20a3bcba4fd01d777c803e90a51227ef586a" :answer/id #uuid "4f9a4ce0-a120-5c6d-bfda-e473791274a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=-2{e}^{-t}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81707/selection/6412317385cfe626b82d69ffde152ec65b94a94d25fa8b2568b90b9ea4bfee4a" :answer/id #uuid "16d6b473-aafc-50ef-8bac-